# WayFinder local configuration  --  copy this file to ".env" and fill it in.
#
# ".env" is git-ignored (it holds secrets); ".env.example" is the committed template.
# The app reads ".env" from the project root at startup (spring.config.import in application.properties), so
# start it from the project root:  ./mvnw spring-boot:run
# Real environment variables always win over values in this file.
# Format: plain KEY=value lines. Comments only on their own line (no trailing "# ..." after a value).

# --- LLM used to understand natural-language routing requests -------------------------------------------------
# Gemini. Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
# IMPORTANT: with INTENT_LLM_PROVIDER=google-genai the app REFUSES TO START if GEMINI_API_KEY is empty.
# So: paste the key first, THEN remove the "# " in front of INTENT_LLM_PROVIDER. Until then the rest of the API
# works normally and the natural-language endpoints answer 503 "not configured".
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# INTENT_LLM_PROVIDER=google-genai

# Optional: override the Gemini model (default gemini-2.5-flash). Check Google's current model list if it is retired.
# INTENT_LLM_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# --- Other providers (instead of Gemini) ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# INTENT_LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# INTENT_LLM_PROVIDER=openai
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# --- Java heap for the multi-city graph ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Vijayawada-Visakhapatnam graph (~1M nodes) needs roughly 0.5-1 GB. Not read from this file: export it in your
# shell, e.g.  export JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS=-Xmx2g
